{"id": "150104", "revid": "2441334", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=150104", "title": "Brenzone sul Garda", "text": "Brenzone sul Garda (or \"Brenzone\") is in Verona Province, by Lake Garda.\nUnderstand.\nThe municipality is made up of 16 small hamlets spread out across a large territory on the Veronese side of Lake Garda. The municipal area includes part of the Monte Baldo massif.\nGet in.\nBy plane.\nVerona Villafranca Airport (), also known as Valerio Catullo Airport, is the closest airport.\nBy car.\nThe SR 249 \"Gardesana Orientale\" passes along the town, which connects lower Lake Garda with the towns of upper Garda in Trentino, including Riva del Garda and Arco, both located a few kilometers from the northern shore of Lake Garda."}
